            {
                "comment": "Jacob ruined my interest in Mechanics. I don't know if it was the material that made the class so bad or if it was him, but he definitely didn't help. Lectures were pretty dry, but the worst part was the homeworks were very hard. Almost no guidance on them and not super similar to TB or lecture examples. He seemed confused if you didn't understand",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 2
            },
            {
                "comment": "Difficult course. Good professor. Homework is long and challenging but graded leniently. Exams are challenging but straightforward. Needs to restructure his office hours format - too many students waiting in the hall. Other than that solid class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Jacob doesn't seem like he wants to be in class, just talks a lot about his note sheet and how smart he is. Homework takes 6-8 hours per assignment and tests are tough. Does not curve the class :(",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 2
            },
            {
                "comment": "Great lecturer and very nice. Possibly the most challenging EMA 506 professor however. His exams are fair with reasonable averages around 80%. His homework assignment are very difficult, start them early and make sure to attend office hours. He is extremely helpful in office hours and they are the key to understanding the hw and course material.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Very competent professor in the sense that he explains difficult concepts both efficiently and effectively. Very helpful with questions and has good examples. He is extremely thorough with his lectures without them coming across as rigorous. I highly recommend Professor Notbohm.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "He is a good professor and makes the material clear, he just does not seem like he wants to be there. He acts like he is above this class and has better things to be doing.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "He's a very reasonable guy and fairly good teacher: a safe bet if you're in a toss-up. I ended up having to miss assignments (extenuating circumstances) and he was very reasonable and easy to work with. Textbook solutions *do* exist for the homework, so ask around. If you pay attention and can complete problems, there's no need to get the textbook.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
